The replay meta-harness was stale: missing tn36 entirely (the program-editor
class solved FRAME-ONLY end-to-end, L1-L7), plus the ar25/ka59 E3 world-model
solves. Cycling all banked solves into one offline scorecard now reports 22
levels across 15 games (was 13/12).

The frame approach is the standout: tn36 replays cleanly to L7 — 7 of the 22
levels, more than the next six games combined (the rest are graph-explore L1
first-solves; lp85 L3). Added load_actions support for the E3
plan_executed_detail.plan_result.executed_steps path so ar25/ka59 replay.

Known remaining undercounts vs the registry's 24: sc25 replays to L0 (its
cast-grid string encoding + first-step warmup aren't handled by the generic
replay) and lp85 shows L3 not L4 (the L4 action list isn't stored flat) — both
need custom per-game replay handling, separate from the frame-approach question.
Offline, air-gapped, zero quota, nothing submitted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
